<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Newton returns three weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg and a month after removal from exposure. Mild nausea in the first few days settled; he has had no other side effects and has missed no doses. He has had three sessions of cognitive behavioral therapy. He sleeps about five and a half hours, keeps the sleep window, and no longer dozes in the evening. He eats three meals a day. He has written to apologize to the friends he accused and has had warm replies; he no longer believes anyone was plotting against him. He is teaching fully and has begun to answer letters again. He has had no thoughts of death or of harming himself or anyone else. The safety office has not yet re-measured the laboratory after its cleaning, so it remains closed. He brought his 24-hour urine collection this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg for three weeks; no side effects now</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Three CBT sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About five and a half hours; no evening dozing</td></tr><tr><td>Suspicious ideas</td><td>Resolved; apologies made and accepted</td></tr><tr><td>Exposure</td><td>None for a month; laboratory still closed</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>14, down from 20</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

